  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Eugene Kellner is the book artist's father.  She reproduces his hand-written story of internment in Nazi concentration camps and translates it on facing pages. The text is printed over family and historic photographs.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The replica of a human arm, made of hand-made paper, rises through the die-cut pages of the book. The number B-11226, resembling a tattoo, is written on the arm.</subfield>
  </datafield>
